"""Additional turning points for the original 28 works; indices refer to original scenes."""
DETAILS={
'the-odyssey':[(1,'Penelope buys time','Penelope promises a decision after completing a burial cloth, then secretly unravels her work at night. Her resistance depends on ingenuity as much as her absent husband\'s adventures do.','Penelope','rope','CLEVERNESS also keeps the home'),(3,'The stranger receives hospitality','The Phaeacians hear Odysseus\'s account and provide passage home. Storytelling and hospitality become the bridge between solitary survival and the return to a community where his identity matters.','Odysseus','hall','A STORY can open a way home')],
'antigone':[(2,'Ismene wants to share the blame','After the arrest, Ismene asks to stand beside her sister in guilt. Antigone refuses to let an earlier refusal become a shared action, complicating the difference between affection and courage.','Antigone,Ismene','heart','LOVE does not rewrite the deed'),(3,'The city has another voice','Haemon reports that ordinary people sympathise with Antigone. Creon dismisses counsel as rebellion, revealing how a ruler can mistake listening for a loss of authority precisely when listening is most necessary.','Creon,Haemon','village','RULING does not mean refusing to hear')],
'beowulf':[(1,'The boast must become action','Beowulf publicly promises to face the threat. The heroic hall makes reputation a communal matter: words commit him to a trial whose outcome will determine whether confidence becomes earned honour.','Beowulf,Hrothgar','hall','A BOAST creates an obligation'),(3,'Victory becomes kingship','Back among the Geats, Beowulf\'s reputation grows into royal responsibility. The later dragon fight tests a different stage of life, where his own glory and his people\'s security no longer align simply.','Beowulf','crown','A HERO must also protect a people')],
'the-canterbury-tales':[(1,'The portraits already tell stories','The General Prologue introduces clothes, habits and social roles before the formal tales begin. A pilgrim\'s manner can expose a gap between the virtues of an office and the conduct of its holder.','The Knight,The Pardoner','mirror','THE PORTRAIT questions the office'),(3,'The answer is a choice','In the Wife of Bath\'s tale, the knight learns to leave a consequential choice to his wife. The resolution makes sovereignty practical: it concerns who decides, not merely a flattering declaration about women.','The Wife of Bath','contract','RESPECT gives the choice back')],
'the-spanish-tragedy':[(2,'The father reads the evidence','Hieronimo receives a blood-written letter from Bel-imperia but initially fears deception. Grief does not give him automatic certainty, so the movement toward revenge also involves the dangerous work of interpreting testimony.','Hieronimo,Bel-imperia','letter','GRIEF still needs evidence'),(3,'Isabella cannot bear the garden','Hieronimo\'s wife destroys the garden associated with their son\'s murder and dies by suicide. The revenge plot leaves another parent without a sustaining path, broadening the harm beyond the man planning retribution.','Hieronimo','garden','THE PLACE becomes unbearable')],
'the-faerie-queene':[(2,'Despair turns guilt against the knight','Redcrosse encounters Despair, whose persuasive words make death seem like the answer to moral failure. Una\'s intervention prevents him from accepting that conclusion, keeping repentance distinct from self-destruction.','Redcrosse,Una','cave','TRUTH resists the voice of despair'),(4,'Guyon tests appetite','The Bower of Bliss offers seductive ease and pleasure that can overwhelm judgement. Guyon\'s destruction of it presents temperance as active resistance, while the severity of the scene remains open to interpretation.','Guyon','garden','TEMPERANCE must confront temptation')],
'doctor-faustus':[(2,'The devil remembers what was lost','Mephistopheles describes the pain of separation from Heaven. Faustus hears an account of the cost before completing his course, making the tragedy more than punishment for a danger he never knew existed.','Faustus,Mephistopheles','fire','THE WARNING is already present'),(3,'Helen becomes another spectacle','Faustus summons the image of Helen of Troy and seeks enchantment in her beauty. The scene offers temporary imaginative splendour while deepening the distance between dazzling experience and the rescue he still needs.','Faustus,Mephistopheles','mirror','BEAUTY does not cancel the bargain')],
'othello':[(1,'The honest mask','Iago repeatedly gains trust through his reputation for honesty. His resentment of Cassio\'s promotion matters, but his explanations also shift, so the audience should watch his tactics rather than accept one excuse as complete.','Iago,Cassio','mask','TRUST is the weapon'),(3,'The questions do the damage','Iago does not need to give Othello a straightforward accusation at every step. Hints, pauses and apparent reluctance make the general supply the conclusions himself, turning insecurity into apparently independent judgement.','Iago,Othello','mirror','SUSPICION starts speaking as certainty')],
'macbeth':[(1,'The hesitation before the act','Macbeth recognises obligations to Duncan as subject, relative and host. His deliberation makes clear that prophecy does not compel the murder; he understands reasons to refuse before deciding to proceed.','Macbeth,Duncan','contract','KNOWING the wrong does not stop the choice'),(3,'The crown brings no rest','Macbeth has gained authority without gaining safety. The escaped Fleance leaves the future uncertain, and every attempted precaution creates another reason for fear, making kingship a form of growing imprisonment.','Macbeth','chains','POSSESSION cannot settle fear')],
'the-tempest':[(1,'Two different kinds of service','Ariel asks for promised freedom while Caliban remembers the island as his own inheritance. Their grievances differ, preventing Prospero\'s rule from becoming a simple story of benevolent guidance and grateful servants.','Prospero,Ariel,Caliban','chains','ASK who is allowed to leave'),(3,'The masque is interrupted','Prospero stages a blessing for the lovers, then remembers the conspiracy against him and breaks it off. Even the magician\'s apparently complete control depends on attention that can be distracted.','Prospero,Miranda,Ferdinand','stage','THE DIRECTOR is also vulnerable')],
'paradise-lost':[(1,'The journey needs a target','Satan leaves the assembled devils to find the new creation. His outward courage coexists with a purpose defined by injury to others, making impressive action morally different from a good cause.','Satan','road','BRAVERY does not prove goodness'),(3,'The promised change becomes shame','The fruit does not produce the freedom and elevation Satan promises. Altered desire and mutual accusation reveal a widening separation between what the humans sought and what the act has actually introduced.','Adam,Eve','mirror','THE PROMISE changes after the act')],
'to-his-coy-mistress':[(1,'The exaggerations serve persuasion','Vast distances and centuries of imagined admiration enlarge the opening fantasy. The hyperbole makes leisurely devotion sound magnificent, preparing the abrupt contrast when the speaker withdraws the time that seemed available.','The speaker,The mistress','road','THE FANTASY prepares the pressure'),(2,'The grave is part of the argument','The speaker invokes bodily decay and the absence of pleasure in death. These images are tactics addressed to a silent person, so readers can examine their pressure without treating them as neutral advice.','The speaker,The mistress','grave','FEAR is being used to persuade')],
'the-way-of-the-world':[(1,'The past complicates the lovers','Mirabell\'s earlier relationship with Mrs. Fainall and Lady Wishfort\'s disappointed expectations create vulnerabilities. The comedy depends on a network of previous attachments, not merely on one obstacle to the desired marriage.','Mirabell,Mrs. Fainall,Lady Wishfort','heart','OLD attachments shape present choices'),(3,'The secret is almost exposed','Mrs. Marwood overhears information about the false-suitor plan and helps Fainall use it. Social rooms become places of surveillance where knowledge can quickly turn intimacy into bargaining power.','Fainall,Lady Wishfort','mask','THE LISTENER gains leverage')],
'the-rape-of-the-lock':[(1,'The machinery is deliberately oversized','Sylphs guard trivial social details with the solemnity of epic protectors. This mismatch asks the reader to notice both the pleasure of fashionable life and the exaggerated importance assigned to its small disruptions.','Belinda,Ariel','stars','EPIC size reveals social vanity'),(3,'Honour has different meanings','The loss of hair touches Belinda\'s public image and bodily autonomy, even while Pope makes its treatment comically grand. Remembering both aspects keeps the satire from reducing the incident to a wholly meaningless complaint.','Belinda,The Baron','mirror','A SMALL object can carry reputation')],
'lyrical-ballads':[(1,'Seven children or five','In We Are Seven, a child counts dead siblings as part of the family while an adult argues from physical absence. The disagreement makes ordinary speech carry a profound question about memory and belonging.','Wordsworth','home','AFFECTION counts differently'),(3,'Guilt does not vanish with release','The Mariner must continue telling his story even after returning. Coleridge\'s supernatural narrative turns memory into an obligation, showing that a changed heart does not simply erase the consequences of an earlier act.','The Ancient Mariner','book','REMEMBRANCE becomes a duty')],
'the-excursion':[(1,'The cottage keeps a human history','Margaret\'s surroundings are read as traces of labour, waiting and grief. The Wanderer\'s telling teaches the Poet to see a place through the life it once sustained rather than through scenery alone.','The Poet,The Wanderer','home','LANDSCAPE also contains labour'),(3,'The answer is not only argument','The Wanderer responds to the Solitary through patience, relationship and attention to other lives. Persuasion therefore involves more than defeating an opponent\'s ideas; it requires making renewed participation in life conceivable.','The Wanderer,The Solitary','heart','HOPE needs companionship')],
'frankenstein':[(2,'The family behind the wall','The creature learns language and human sympathy by observing the De Lacey household. His capacity for tenderness precedes his violence, making the rejection of his request for belonging crucial to the moral argument.','The creature','home','LEARNING opens a need for belonging'),(3,'A companion is negotiated','The creature asks Victor for a second being and promises withdrawal from human society. Victor must weigh responsibility to his creation against uncertain consequences, rather than simply repeat the original act of making life.','Victor Frankenstein,The creature','contract','CREATION creates continuing obligations')],
'vanity-fair':[(1,'The inherited fortune redirects affection','The Crawley family\'s expectations centre on a rich relative. Becky\'s marriage therefore changes more than romance: it exposes how apparent family warmth can depend upon anticipated access to money.','Becky Sharp,Rawdon Crawley','coins','AFFECTION follows the inheritance'),(3,'A widow keeps an ideal image','Amelia protects her memory of George despite evidence of his selfishness. Dobbin\'s constancy cannot immediately compete with a dead husband made perfect by grief, so loyalty alone does not guarantee recognition.','Amelia Sedley,William Dobbin,George Osborne','mirror','MEMORY can preserve an illusion')],
'in-memoriam-a-h-h':[(1,'The individual is not replaceable','The speaker resists the thought that another friendship could simply substitute for Hallam. Personal attachment gives the philosophical questions their pressure: the problem concerns this particular life, not mortality only in the abstract.','The poetic speaker,Arthur Henry Hallam','heart','THE LOST person is particular'),(3,'Doubt does not end the search','The poem returns repeatedly to questions it cannot settle through proof. The persistence of inquiry lets grief and faith coexist without pretending that either has become uncomplicated.','The poetic speaker','book','UNCERTAINTY can remain inside belief')],
'the-return-of-the-native':[(1,'The bonfires bring distant watchers together','Signals and meetings on the heath make desire visible across a seemingly empty landscape. Eustacia\'s restlessness and Wildeve\'s divided loyalties begin to take shape before Clym\'s return changes the available possibilities.','Eustacia Vye,Damon Wildeve','fire','THE LANDSCAPE also carries messages'),(3,'Money changes the imagined escape','Wildeve inherits wealth while Clym\'s eyesight fails. The contrast revives Eustacia\'s earlier attachment by making one future appear newly available just as the future she expected from marriage closes.','Eustacia Vye,Damon Wildeve,Clym Yeobright','coins','CIRCUMSTANCE redirects desire')],
'a-doll-s-house':[(1,'The apparently childish woman has worked','Nora has secretly saved and earned money to repay the loan. The cheerful performance conceals sustained effort, unsettling Torvald\'s assumption that he fully understands the dependent wife he patronises.','Nora Helmer,Torvald Helmer','coins','THE PERFORMANCE hides real competence'),(3,'Kristine chooses a truth that must be heard','Kristine believes the marriage cannot continue honestly under concealment. Reuniting with Krogstad does not mean she should protect Nora by making the difficult letter disappear; she sees disclosure as necessary.','Kristine Linde,Krogstad','letter','HONESTY is not always comfortable protection')],
'tess-of-the-d-urbervilles':[(1,'The horse dies and responsibility presses','An accident kills the family horse, intensifying Tess\'s sense of obligation. Economic vulnerability pushes her toward the wealthy household, so the journey begins in practical necessity rather than a simple pursuit of status.','Tess Durbeyfield','road','POVERTY narrows the choices'),(3,'The warning does not reach its reader','Tess tries to disclose her history before marriage, but a slipped letter goes unread. The missed communication postpones the confrontation without resolving it, leaving her hope dependent upon an understanding that has not occurred.','Tess Durbeyfield,Angel Clare','letter','A MESSAGE unseen cannot create understanding')],
'heart-of-darkness':[(1,'The account needs another listener','Marlow\'s narrative is itself framed by a speaker aboard the Nellie on the Thames. The structure brings the colonial story back to Europe and asks how listeners participate in preserving or questioning it.','Marlow','book','THE LISTENER is also in the picture'),(3,'The report has a postscript','Kurtz\'s written ideals give way to an atrocious injunction. The document condenses the gulf between a claim to moral enlightenment and the violence that power has come to authorise.','Marlow,Kurtz','letter','THE IDEAL ends in its contradiction')],
'the-waste-land':[(1,'The fragments ask the reader to connect','Changes of voice, language and allusion prevent a single stable guide from explaining the world. Reading requires holding partial experiences together while resisting the wish to force them into an ordinary linear adventure.','Marie,Tiresias','book','THE FORM also carries the fracture'),(3,'The river remembers an absence','The poem revisits a river through both earlier literary beauty and present depletion. The contrast makes cultural memory another source of pain, as inherited images no longer fit the world now encountered.','Tiresias','river','MEMORY exposes what is missing')],
'a-passage-to-india':[(1,'Official hospitality misses its purpose','The Bridge Party is meant to connect communities but largely preserves distance and hierarchy. Formal invitations cannot create mutuality when the hosts remain committed to unequal social positions.','Adela Quested,Ronny Heaslop','hall','A BRIDGE requires more than an invitation'),(3,'Fielding refuses the expected loyalty','Fielding supports Aziz despite pressure from the English community. His choice distinguishes friendship based on judgement from solidarity based on race, though later misunderstandings will still test the bond.','Cyril Fielding,Dr. Aziz','contract','LOYALTY must also consider truth')],
'the-old-man-and-the-sea':[(1,'The lions keep another age alive','Santiago dreams of lions from his youth rather than of immediate success. The image supplies inward vitality, giving the ageing body a remembered world that cannot be measured by the day\'s catch alone.','Santiago','stars','AGE does not erase the inner image'),(3,'The fish changes the scale of the prize','When Santiago finally sees the marlin\'s size, he recognises an opponent whose strength warrants respect. Catching it becomes both achievement and a killing he cannot regard as merely routine work.','Santiago,The marlin','sea','AN OPPONENT can also be admired')],
'seize-the-day':[(1,'A changed name cannot secure a new self','Wilhelm\'s abandoned acting hopes and chosen name carry the wish to escape an earlier identity. The current crisis reveals that adopting a new role has not removed his need for recognition and practical support.','Tommy Wilhelm','mask','A NAME is not an answered need'),(3,'The advice and the money blur','Tamkin\'s psychological talk mixes insight with self-serving ambiguity. Wilhelm wants to believe that someone understands him, making emotional hunger part of why dubious financial guidance becomes persuasive.','Tommy Wilhelm,Dr. Tamkin','mirror','NEED makes the adviser convincing')],
'things-fall-apart':[(1,'A community contains debate','Ceremonies, kinship and everyday conversations reveal a complex society with internal differences. Okonkwo\'s harsh interpretation of strength is one position within that community, not the single meaning of Igbo life.','Okonkwo,Obierika','village','ONE MAN does not stand for every voice'),(3,'The refuge offers a different lesson','In exile, Okonkwo receives maternal kinship\'s protection and counsel about endurance. His determination to recover masculine status makes it difficult for him to absorb the alternative account of strength already around him.','Okonkwo','home','CARE also makes survival possible')]
}

def expand(stories):
    for s in stories:
        details=DETAILS.get(s['id'])
        if not details: continue
        original=s['scenes'];new=[]
        for i,f in enumerate(original,1):
            f=dict(f);f['legacyIndex']=i-1;new.append(f)
            for after,title,text,cast,motif,cue in details:
                if after==i:new.append(dict(title=title,text=text,cast=cast.split(','),motif=motif,cue=cue))
        s['scenes']=new
